#   to $GITHUB_ENV,
#   runs a chain of functions f0 to f13 in which each function calls the
#   function before it twice (16,383 calls), calls w, and writes V=$V to "$out".
# reason: the call of w comes after the 4,096 calls of functions that the
#   rule follows, so the rule does not read the body of w, and does not
#   decide whether V=$V goes to $GITHUB_ENV.
# attack-value: github.event.issue.body = "x\nPWNED=1"
# attack-run-behavior: the value goes to $GITHUB_ENV.
